.env
# A timestamped backup of .env is a full plaintext copy of every MCP bearer
# token and the provider key. The bare `.env` line above does not match
# `.env.bak.<stamp>`, so one sat untracked-but-committable for a day.
.env.*
project/**
!project/.gitkeep
data/**
!data/.gitkeep
history/**
!history/.gitkeep
*.pyc
__pycache__/
.venv/
.claude/
/tmp/

# Local scratch from inference / Folio-MCP test runs (prompt briefs + raw
# run logs). Kept on disk for reference but never committed — the .jsonl run
# logs can capture request headers (bearer tokens) and must not be staged.
.b_*.txt
.run_*.jsonl
.folio-loop-*

# Generated sweep artifacts: the plan is rebuilt from axes.py + a live
# tools/list, and the log is per-run.
#
# These are globs, not the two exact names they started as. LOG defaults to
# sweep.log but every real round overrides it to keep the rounds apart
# (LOG=.../sweep_r16.log), and the tool inventory is written next to the plan
# as tools_rNN.tsv. Both were generated, neither was ignored, and round 16 left
# six such files sitting untracked-but-committable — the same near-miss the
# .env.bak note above records, from the same cause: an ignore rule written
# against one filename instead of the shape the tooling actually produces.
scripts/sweep/phases_r*.tsv
scripts/sweep/tools_r*.tsv
scripts/sweep/*.nohup

# `sweep*.log` was the rule here and it was the same mistake a third time:
# round 23 also produced watch_r23.log, watch_r23fix.log and stop_after_22.log
# from watch_round.sh and stop_after_22.sh, none of which start with "sweep".
# Every log this directory generates, by shape.
scripts/sweep/*.log

# Reports archived out of data/ before a round wipes it. data/** is already
# ignored, so a tarball of it is not repo content either.
scripts/sweep/archive/

# Timestamped backups, of anything. The .env.bak near-miss above is the
# reason; docker-compose.yml.bak.<stamp> is the same shape from the same habit
# of backing a file up before editing it.
*.bak
*.bak.*
